From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Simon Elsbrock <simon@iodev.org>
Date: Thu, 26 Nov 2026 12:45:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] arm: dts: mediatek: run the Echo Dot (5th gen) SDIO at 50 MHz

At SDR104 (200 MHz) the MT7663 accepted its ROM patch and N9 firmware over
SDIO, then answered no command: mt7663s timed out starting the N9 firmware
and btmtksdio timed out enabling Bluetooth, on cold and warm starts, with
SDIO interrupts or polling. In high speed mode at 50 MHz both start, and
Bluetooth scans (C2N6L4, 2026-11-26). Drop the UHS modes until SDR104
tuning works on this host.

---
--- a/arch/arm/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8519-amzn.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/boot/dts/mediatek/mt8519-amzn.dtsi
@@ -103,12 +103,14 @@
 	pinctrl-3 = <&mmc1_pins_dat1>;
 	eint-gpios = <&pio 79 0>;
 	bus-width = <4>;
-	max-frequency = <200000000>;
+	/*
+	 * High speed at 50 MHz. At SDR104 the MT7663 took its firmware but
+	 * answered no command once it ran: Wi-Fi's N9 start and Bluetooth's
+	 * WMT enable timed out (C2N6L4, 2026-11-26).
+	 */
+	max-frequency = <50000000>;
 	cap-sd-highspeed;
 	cap-sdio-async-int;
-	sd-uhs-sdr104;
-	sd-uhs-sdr50;
-	sd-uhs-sdr25;
 	keep-power-in-suspend;
 	enable-sdio-wakeup;
 	cap-sdio-irq;
